
# Mini Redis in Java

A lightweight, Redis-inspired in-memory key-value store built
from scratch using Java 25.

## Features

- Key-value operations: SET, GET, DEL, EXISTS
- TTL-based key expiration
- TCP client-server communication
- Concurrent client handling with Java virtual threads
- Snapshot persistence to disk
- Manual and scheduled snapshot saving

## Tech Stack

- Java 25
- TCP sockets
- ConcurrentHashMap
- Java concurrency utilities
- File I/O and Base64 encoding

## Run Locally

Compile the source files:

```bash
javac MiniRedis.java RedisServer.java RedisClient.java
```

Start the server:

```bash
java RedisServer
```

In another terminal, start the client:

```bash
java RedisClient
```

## Example Commands

```text
SET language Java
GET language
SET username Diksha EX 60
TTL username
SAVE
```

## Current Limitations

This is an educational project inspired by Redis.
It uses a simplified line-based TCP protocol and is not
fully compatible with standard Redis clients.
